<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gerard Lake, 1st Viscount Lake</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1744">1744</a>–<a href="/years/1808">1808</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Lord Lake</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gerard Lake, 1st Viscount Lake, was a British general who became commander-in-chief in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1801. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-anglo-maratha-war">Second Anglo-Maratha War</a> he defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> and Laswari in 1803, bringing Delhi and the Mughal emperor under British protection. In 1805 he failed to take the fort of Bharatpur after four assaults. He rewarded allies with grants such as the state of Dujana.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gerard-lake-1st-viscount-lake.jpg" alt="Gerard Lake, 1st Viscount Lake" width="264" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to George Place · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gerard_Lake.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
